# Nothing is tracked unless it is named here.
#
# This started as a deny-list and that was the wrong shape. The working folder holds 21.6 GB of
# agent scratch across 156,348 files - full copies of the application, npm caches, generated import
# fixtures, a 231 MB probe result - and a deny-list against that is a list you lose. First attempt
# staged 927 MB.
#
# So: ignore everything, then name what belongs. Anything new an agent drops in the tree is invisible
# to git until somebody decides otherwise, which is the correct default for this project.
#
# The rule for deciding: track what is DURABLE and TEXT. The patch scripts, the harnesses, the
# briefs, the handbacks, the docs. Every application build is reproducible by replaying the tracked
# scripts against the frozen base its APPLY_ORDER.md names - if a build cannot be reproduced that
# way, that is a defect in the round, not a reason to commit the artefact.

*
!*/

# ---- the documents that say what this is ----------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!AGENT_CONVENTIONS.md
!RESUME_HERE.md
!mpl.txt

# ---- the patch scripts: how every release was actually built ---------------------------------
!tools/**/*.py
!tools/**/*.js

# ---- the verification harnesses: how every claim was proved ----------------------------------
!qa_exports/*.js

# ---- the briefs, the handbacks, and the pinned patch chains -----------------------------------
!codex/*.md
!codex/*.txt
!codex/round*_patches/**/*.js
!codex/round*_patches/**/*.md
!antigravity/*.md
!antigravity/*.txt
!audit/*.md

# ---- design work in progress ------------------------------------------------------------------
!pending/wonders/*.md
!pending/wonders/*.py
!pending/wonders/wonders_scene.html
!pending/thememenu/*.md
!pending/thememenu/*.py

# ---- the shipped application ------------------------------------------------------------------
# From 1.69.0 onward, which is where this repository starts. The 62 earlier snapshots stay on disk
# in releases/ and backups/; importing 343 MB of history nobody will check out would make every
# clone pay for it, and how each was BUILT is tracked above.
!releases/SIREN_v1.69.0.html
!releases/SIREN_v1.70.0.html

# ---- the status page --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The source of the published worklist artifact. It lived only in a session scratchpad, which is
# temporary; the artifact is the thing everybody reads, so its source belongs with the project.
!siren_worklist.html
!siren_interface_report.html
!siren_plan.html
!docs/**/*.md
!.claude/skills/**/*.md

